Subject: [PATCH] SLEIGH: expose a decision node's field

Ghidra's Java disassembler records, for each instruction, the bits that
selected its constructors (SleighDebugLogger: the instruction mask and
the operand masks an InstructionPrototype reports). Each DecisionNode
on the way to a constructor contributes the field it decides on. A tool
that computes the same masks over the C++ engine (Function ID hashes,
which mask operands out of instructions) needs the field each node reads.

Add read-only accessors: DecisionNode::isContextDecision, getStartBit and
getBitSize. No behaviour changes.

Seen in: revkit's Function ID (src/fid). Ghidra 12.1.4.

diff --git a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/slghsymbol.hh b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/slghsymbol.hh
index eb5a963..682679c 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/slghsymbol.hh
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/slghsymbol.hh
@@ -585,6 +585,9 @@ public:
   void decode(Decoder &decoder,DecisionNode *par,SubtableSymbol *sub);
   const vector<pair<DisjointPattern *,Constructor *> > &getPairs(void) const { return list; }	///< (pattern, constructor) pairs held here
   const vector<DecisionNode *> &getChildren(void) const { return children; }	///< Sub-decisions
+  bool isContextDecision(void) const { return contextdecision; }	///< Whether the decision reads context bits rather than instruction bits
+  int4 getStartBit(void) const { return startbit; }	///< First bit the decision reads
+  int4 getBitSize(void) const { return bitsize; }	///< Bits the decision reads (0: a leaf, decided by its patterns)
 };
 
 class SubtableSymbol : public TripleSymbol {
